  "The buffer is needed because people can immediately recall about 16 words from a meaningful sentence, more than their span for unrelated words, since meaning and long-term language knowledge let the words stay connected. Some amnesic patients can immediately recall a just-heard story, which suggests immediate retention of an organized episode can survive when longer-term memory is impaired.",
  "A sentence's words are kept together as connected material, not as 16 separate items.",
